## Hydrogen Evolution Reaction
Decorated for HER: Using the open porosity derived from the pyrolysis of metal–organic frameworks (MOFs), ${\mathsf{M o O}}_{2}$ small nanoparticles can be deposited in the porous carbon by chemical vapor deposition. Carbonization, nitridation, or phosphorization, selectively gives ${\mathsf{M o}}_{2}{\mathsf{C}}.$ , MoN-, and MoP-decorated carbocatalysts with unchanged morphology. The catalysts are promising for the hydrogen evolution reaction.
